#### WE LOOK FORWARD TO SEEING YOU AT CAMP!

#### READ ON FOR MORE INFORMATION

## Reminders For Everyone

* **ALWAYS CARRY YOUR FLASHLIGHT!** Don't forget to bring a FLASHLIGHT or HEADLAMP & spare batteries!
* There is no WIFI at camp. If you have Verizon as your phone provider, you might be able to make a call or send a text out in one location at camp (ask us when you're there), but there's not enough signal strength to be able to read or send email. If someone needs to reach you for a genuine emergency, they can call the Mendocino Woodlands office. Their staff will relay a message to our staff, and we'll track you down.
* You will want your phone for photos and recording at workshops, and possibly alarms and reminders, but there are limited places to plug in and recharge. Please, be responsible about removing your phone from where you're charging so others can have a chance to do so, too. You might consider bringing a battery bank or a solar phone charger.
* As noted in our last newsletter, bears have been seen recently at camp. In addition, mice, chipmunks, skunks and racoons are ever present in the redwoods. These critters have "a particular set of skills" when it comes to food. Do not store or eat food in your car, cabin, or tent!
* Bring your mosquito/tick repellent! Those in the know say it's a big year for the bugs at camp.
* **Fire rules:** No candles, stoves, or lanterns with flames! Break this rule once and you will be ejected from camp. $250.00 fine! Help keep us all safe!
* Park where you are assigned, in the proper fire exit direction. Cars parked incorrectly will be towed away at the owner's expense.
* When driving, do not exceed 5 MPH and use headlights for safety. This keeps dust down and people safe!
* Bike riding ON THE ROAD ONLY. Walk your bike on any other paths.
* Do not store personal items in bathhouses.
* Parents must take full responsibility for their children at all times and in all situations.
* No pets allowed (for everyone's safety). $250.00 fine for breaking this rule.
* **LARK CAMP ASSUMES NO RESPONSIBILITY FOR PERSONAL BELONGINGS OR VEHICLES.**

## CARPOOLING

Please offer rides to campers! We have some folks who are still hoping to carpool to camp, including crew members who need to arrive on Thursday. Parking passes are refundable, so carpooling has benefits! [Post a ride request or offer](https://groupcarpool.com/t/usfk0v)

## REGARDING WATER & SHOWERS

Water in the Woodlands comes from a tank that is fed by a well. This means water is limited! Please take VERY short and infrequent showers.

{% if 'Cabin' in lodging -%}
### CABIN LODGING

* No nails, pushpins, or staples in any building or cabin. Preserve our historic buildings.
* Leave your cabin or camping area perfectly clean! Another group moves into the Woodlands as we move out. Help our volunteers by not creating extra work for them. You can find brooms in bathroom storerooms.

{% endif -%}
## IF YOU ARE NEW TO LARK CAMP

We suggest arriving early (that is, anytime AFTER 3:00pm) to have time to get settled in before it's dark in an unfamiliar place.

**CAMP 1 Newcomer Orientation** Saturday at 8:30am & Tuesday at 6:00pm (meet on or near the steps outside the office).

**CAMP 2 Newcomer Orientation** Saturday at 8:30am & Tuesday at 6:00pm (meet at the inner fire circle by the Coffeehouse).

## WORK TRADE POSITIONS

All Work Trade Crews are full.

If you are signed up for camp, the kitchen may have availability to allow you to wash dishes, etc. in trade for meals. Contact our caterer at: [larkkitchen@gmail.com](mailto:larkkitchen@gmail.com)

